1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:07,840
My wife and I wanted to share our new home with family and friends by hosting a small gathering in the early summer.
我和妻子想在初夏办个小型聚会，和亲朋好友一起分享我们的新家。

2
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:13,110
She had prepared lots of snacks, while my job was to have the backyard in order.
她准备了很多零食，而我的任务是把后院收拾妥当。

3
00:00:13,910 --> 00:00:16,570
There was plenty of space for the kids to run and play.
那里有足够的空间让孩子们跑来跑去、尽情玩耍。

4
00:00:17,370 --> 00:00:23,790
There was just one thing I hadn’t counted on: My brother chose to bring his dog Toby, a 50-pound ball of fire.
只有一件事出乎我的预料：弟弟选择带上了他的狗托比，一个五十磅重、精力旺盛的小家伙。

5
00:00:24,590 --> 00:00:30,410
Though friendly, he could easily knock over my niece’s small boys and my six-month-old granddaughter.
托比虽然友好，却很容易撞倒外甥女家的小男孩们和我六个月大的孙女。

6
00:00:31,210 --> 00:00:35,710
So, when my brother showed up, I asked him to watch Toby and keep him outside.
所以，弟弟一来，我就让他看好托比，把它留在外面。

7
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:38,380
My plan was working out just fine.
我的计划进展得十分顺利。

8
00:00:39,180 --> 00:00:45,040
Toby was using up his energy by running back and forth in the backyard and giving the kids plenty of room.
托比在后院跑来跑去，消耗着体力，也给孩子们留出了足够的空间。

9
00:00:45,840 --> 00:00:48,900
Unexpectedly, after supper, the weather changed.
没想到，晚饭后天气变了。

10
00:00:49,700 --> 00:00:52,170
It started to rain and everyone went indoors.
天开始下雨，大家都进了屋。

11
00:00:52,970 --> 00:00:54,270
It was an awkward moment.
那一刻十分尴尬。

12
00:00:55,070 --> 00:01:01,090
I didn’t want Toby to be running around in the house, and my brother wasn’t happy with driving home with a wet dog.
我不想让托比在屋里到处乱跑，弟弟也不乐意带着一条湿漉漉的狗开车回家。

13
00:01:01,890 --> 00:01:05,470
Eventually, my brother decided to leave rather than force the issue.
最终，弟弟决定一走了之，而不是硬要把这件事闹僵。

14
00:01:06,270 --> 00:01:09,810
A few days passed, and I hadn’t heard anything from my brother.
几天过去了，我一直没有弟弟的音信。

15
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:14,000
I texted him and expressed wishes for him to come out again.
我给他发短信，表示希望他再来玩。

16
00:01:14,800 --> 00:01:19,210
His reply came as a surprise—a shock, actually: “Not a chance.”
他的回复让我很意外——其实是震惊：“没门儿。”

17
00:01:20,010 --> 00:01:22,730
Clearly, he was unhappy over the way we had parted.
显然，他还在为我们那天不欢而散而不高兴。

18
00:01:23,530 --> 00:01:26,110
After all, I had left him little choice.
毕竟，我当时没给他留多少选择余地。

19
00:01:26,910 --> 00:01:29,260
Well, he’ll get over it, I reasoned.
唉，他会想通的，我心里这么盘算。

20
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:31,170
Two months passed.
两个月过去了。

21
00:01:31,970 --> 00:01:37,870
My wife suggested I get in touch with my brother, but I resisted, thinking he should call first.
妻子建议我联系一下弟弟，我却不肯，心想该他先打电话来。

22
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:40,900
However, my conscience kept bothering me.
然而，我的良心一直让我不安。

23
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,810
I tried to put myself in my brother’s shoes.
我试着设身处地为弟弟想想。

24
00:01:44,610 --> 00:01:50,120
He was facing health issues and his wife of thirty-five years had passed away a few months earlier.
他身体出了些毛病，和他相伴三十五年的妻子几个月前又去世了。

25
00:01:50,920 --> 00:01:54,400
Toby was his constant companion, the one who kept him going.
托比是他形影不离的伙伴，是支撑他活下去的那个依靠。

26
00:01:55,200 --> 00:01:57,280
I realized it was me who was at fault.
我意识到，错的是我自己。

27
00:01:58,080 --> 00:02:01,750
With the biscuits my wife had made, I arrived at my brother’s door.
我带着妻子做的饼干，来到了弟弟家门口。
